# Architecture Rules

Inherit Project1 (`public-law-ai`) philosophy.

## Boundaries

- `app/knowledge/domain` has **zero outward dependencies**.
- Business logic depends on **ports (interfaces)**, never concrete adapters.
- Only `app/knowledge/composition` may import and wire concrete adapters.
- No upward imports (lower layers never import higher layers).
- Cross-cutting modules (`evaluation`, `observability`, `reliability`,
  `security`) may depend downward; production business modules must not depend
  on them.

## Patterns

- Interfaces before implementations.
- Name concrete adapters `Default*` / `InMemory*` / `Fake*` + interface name.
- Prefer explicit use cases in `application` over god-object services.
- Keep module `index.ts` barrels accurate.

## Task 1 constraint

Do not implement product features in the skeleton phase. Add ports/adapters
only when a later task explicitly scopes them.
